{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor adds configurable ad timeout and concurrency controls for improved ad fill and faster startup - AWS","context":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor, a service offered by Amazon Web Services (AWS), has introduced new features that allow users to configure ad decision server (ADS) timeouts and concurrency controls. Previously, these settings required contacting AWS Support for modifications. The new settings include individual HTTP ad request timeouts, total ad personalization time budgets for live, VOD, and live ad prefetch, and the ability to enable parallel ADS requests. These adjustments enable users to optimize ad delivery performance for their specific workflows. For instance, increasing the personalization time budget for live events can enhance ad fill rates, while enabling parallel ADS requests in VOD workflows can decrease overall response time for faster video startup. Additionally, new prefetch-specific timeout settings offer more granularity for livestream ad retrieval. Users can configure these settings through the AWS Elemental MediaTailor console, AWS CLI, or AWS SDKs using the new AdsPersonalizationTimeouts and AdsPersonalizationConcurrency parameters on playback configurations. This feature is accessible in all AWS Regions where AWS Elemental MediaTailor is available. For more information on configuring ADS request timeouts, personalization time budgets, and concurrency, refer to the Advanced settings section in the AWS Elemental MediaTailor User Guide","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/mediatail-configurable-ad-timeout-and-concurrency/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now supports Low-Latency HLS ad insertion - AWS","context":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now supports low-latency HTTP Live Streaming (LL-HLS) ad insertion using HLS Interstitials. MediaTailor is a service for video providers to monetize live streams, linear channels, and video-on-demand content. LL-HLS reduces live latency by delivering partial segments and keeping media playlists cacheable at CDN edges. MediaTailor uses HLS Interstitials to reference ads as separate playlists, allowing for low-latency playback at scale and moving ad decision server calls off the manifest request path. This capability is ideal for live sports, news, betting and wagering, watch-party, and interactive live formats. Low-latency HLS ad insertion is available in all AWS Regions where MediaTailor is available. For more information, visit the MediaTailor product page and server-guided ad insertion documentation. To get started, sign in to the MediaTailor console. MediaTailor supports LL-HLS by delivering partial segments and keeping media playlists cacheable at CDN edges, using HLS Interstitials to reference ads as separate playlists, and moving ad decision server calls off the manifest request path. This results in low-latency playback at scale, making it suitable for live events and interactive formats where latency is crucial. The feature is currently available in all AWS Regions where MediaTailor is offered. For further details, interested parties can refer to the MediaTailor product page and server-guided ad insertion documentation and sign in to the MediaTailor console to get started","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/aws-elemental-mediatailor-low-latency-hls-ad-insertion/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"resilience-hub-failure-mode-assessment","skill_description":"Runs and interprets AWS Resilience Hub v2 failure mode assessments. Covers starting assessments, understanding findings (severity, categories, recommendations), triaging by achievability, working with AI-generated service functions, and resolving findings. Applies when the user wants to run an assessment, review findings, or understand failure modes, or has a specific finding and asks how to resolve, remediate, or fix it. Does not apply to initial setup (use resilience-hub-getting-started) or FIS experiments.\n\n\nServices: resiliencehub\nTasks: audit, troubleshoot, monitor\nPersona: developer, devops, architect\nWorkload: resilience\n*","skill_name":"resilience-hub-failure-mode-assessment"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"troubleshooting-efs","skill_description":"Diagnoses and resolves Amazon EFS issues including mount failures, NFS timeouts, permission errors, throughput problems, and burst credit exhaustion. Use when the user has an EFS file system that is not mounting, returning errors, performing slowly, or showing access denied.\n\n\nServices: efs, ec2, iam, kms, vpc, cloudwatch\nTasks: debug, troubleshoot, diagnose\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: storage\n*","skill_name":"troubleshooting-efs"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"securing-s3-buckets","skill_description":"Create and secure S3 buckets following AWS best practices for access control, encryption, monitoring, and remediation of misconfigurations. Use when the user wants to secure a new bucket, audit an existing bucket, fix a security finding, configure encryption, or enable logging and monitoring. Do NOT use for general S3 data operations, S3 Tables setup, or discovering existing data assets.\n\n\nServices: s3, kms, cloudtrail, guardduty, config, accessanalyzer\nTasks: secure, audit, remediate, encrypt, monitor\nPersona: developer, security-engineer\nWorkload: storage, compliance\n*","skill_name":"securing-s3-buckets"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Search AWS docs for MediaTailor session expiration causing HTTP 400 errors", "parent_id": "2f7f7e7b-0536-468a-ae05-ebcd99f76862"}

